20% of 50 people is 20/100 * 50 = 10 people. So, 50 - 10 = 40 people remain. 60% of the remaining people (40) think horse #7 will win, so 60/100 * 40 = 24 people think horse #7 will win. The rest of the people (40 - 24 = 16) think horse #12 will win.
Thus, 16 people think horse #12 will win.

The answer is: \boxed{16}

